course: dictionary
lesson: 1709
title: One name, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cinderella with a capital C is a name. It names one special girl in a famous fairy tale, so it is a proper noun, and proper nouns always start with a capital letter.
explain: Look at the words around the word to understand it. «A Chinese Cinderella story, Ye Xian, was written down around 850 CE» tells you the tale is very old and told in many places, so Cinderella is part of a story's title.
explain: Without a capital letter and with «a» in front, a Cinderella is a different kind of word. It means a person or thing that is ignored but deserves more attention. Sports writers also use Cinderella story for a small, unexpected team that does very well.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If a small village team beats the champions, and someone calls it a Cinderella story, the meaning fits, so you have understood it.
fact: Cinderella, as a name, is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Cinderella» is a girl in a famous fairy tale who is treated badly, goes to the prince's ball and loses a glass slipper.
fact: «A Cinderella» (no capital) means a person or thing that is ignored but deserves more attention.
fact: In sport, a «Cinderella story» is when a small, unexpected team or person does very well.
fact: «A Chinese Cinderella story, Ye Xian,» was written down around 850 CE, and similar stories are told in many cultures.
exercise: «A Chinese Cinderella story, Ye Xian, was written down around 850 CE.» What kind of word is Cinderella here? | *A proper noun, a name | An adjective, a describing word | A pronoun, like he or she | A verb, an action word
exercise: Sam says the small school choir that wins the county final is a Cinderella story. What does he mean? | *A small, unexpected group that does very well | A story read aloud at bedtime | A choir that only sings at Christmas | A choir that wins every year and is always expected to
exercise: «The old violin in the corner was a Cinderella: nobody played it, but it deserved more attention.» What does a Cinderella mean here? | *Something ignored that deserves more attention | A glass slipper | A prince at a ball | A quick runner
test: Which word is a name, so it needs a capital letter? | ball | slipper | ancient | *Cinderella
test: In sport, what does «Cinderella story» mean? | A team that loses every game | *A small, unexpected team does very well | A team wearing new shoes | A story read at bedtime
exam: Which sentence uses Cinderella as the name of the fairy-tale girl? | *«Cinderella lost her glass slipper at midnight.» | «The Cinderella team cheered at the final whistle.» | «He felt like a Cinderella in his own class.» | «The team was a Cinderella, ignored all season.»
